# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile did two harmful things:
#
# 1. It baked .env / .env.local — the Azure Voice Live key, the Postgres
#    password and the storage connection string — into an image layer. Anyone
#    who can pull the image can read them, and they persist in the layer even if
#    a later instruction deletes the file. Credentials must arrive at RUNTIME
#    (docker-compose already does this via `env_file`), never at build time.
#
# 2. It copied the HOST's node_modules over the ones just installed by
#    `npm install --production`. The host is Windows and the image is
#    linux/alpine, so any package with a native binding was silently replaced
#    with an incompatible build.
node_modules
npm-debug.log

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# Old pre-migration snapshots — not imported by src/, just dead weight (and
# they were reachable over HTTP until the express.static mount was scoped down).
legacy

# Local scratch
*.log
uploads
recordings
